msgid "Compare avalanche apps"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An honest comparison of the avalanche bulletin apps used across the Alps — "
"WhiteRisk, SnowSafe, Whympr, AvalancheClarity, Skitourenguru and Snowdesk — "
"and which to pick for where you ski."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Nine products that put an avalanche bulletin on your phone, what each one "
"actually does, and which to reach for depending on where you ski. Written by "
"the team behind one of them, and it says so."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">Before any of this.</strong> Every product "
"here is a way of reading a forecast written by somebody else — SLF in "
"Switzerland, Météo-France in France, ALBINA for Austria and northern Italy, "
"and their equivalents elsewhere. The bulletin is the authority. An app that "
"is prettier, faster or better translated does not change what the snowpack "
"is doing, and none of them substitutes for avalanche training, a transceiver "
"you can use, and partners who can use theirs."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose on coverage first, and on how quickly you can read the forecast for "
"where you are actually going. Everything else is secondary."
msgstr ""

msgid "The short answer, by where you ski"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Most people need one app, and which one is decided almost entirely by "
"geography — because coverage is the thing these products differ on most and "
"compromise on least."
msgstr ""

msgid "Switzerland, mostly"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">WhiteRisk.</strong> It is built by SLF, the "
"institute that writes the Swiss bulletin. Nothing else in this list has that."
msgstr ""

msgid "Austria, South Tyrol, Trentino, or the Nordics and Eastern Europe"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">SnowSafe.</strong> Roughly seventeen regions "
"across the Austrian LWDs, Bavaria, northern Italy, Slovenia, Slovakia, "
"Czechia, Poland, Iceland and Norway. No Switzerland and no France."
msgstr ""

msgid "France"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">Yéti</strong> for a tour rated against today's "
"bulletin, or <strong class=\"text-text-1\">AvalancheClarity</strong> if you "
"want the Météo-France bulletin explained in your own language."
msgstr ""

msgid "Crossing borders on the same trip"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">AvalancheClarity</strong> or <strong "
"class=\"text-text-1\">Snowdesk</strong> — both put several countries' "
"bulletins in one place, with different trade-offs between breadth and depth."
msgstr ""

msgid "You want a specific tour scored for today"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">Skitourenguru</strong> for the Alps, or "
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">Yéti</strong> for France. Both are free, and "
"both rate individual routes daily by combining the bulletin with terrain "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

msgid "You are planning the day with other people"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See <a class=\"underline\" href=\"#planning\">planning together</a> below — "
"this is the one dimension where the products differ most and advertise it "
"least."
msgstr ""

msgid "You are chasing snowfall in the US or Canada"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"<strong class=\"text-text-1\">OpenSnow.</strong> A forecast product rather "
"than a bulletin product, and no European avalanche coverage."
msgstr ""

msgid "What each one costs and covers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Prices are as found on the dates given at the foot of this page. Anything "
"marked <span class=\"font-mono text-caption uppercase tracking-wide bg-tag "
"rounded-sm px-1 py-0.5\" >unconfirmed</span> comes from secondary sources "
"rather than the product's own site, because the site could not be reached "
"when the check ran."
msgstr ""

