msgid "1. About Snowdesk"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snowdesk is operated by Hugo Rodger-Brown (\"I\", \"me\", \"my\"), an "
"individual based in London, UK. Snowdesk displays avalanche bulletins "
"published by the WSL Institute for Snow and Avalanche Research (SLF) for "
"Switzerland, by ALBINA / EUREGIO for Tyrol, South Tyrol and Trentino, and by "
"Météo-France for the French mountain ranges. It publishes no avalanche "
"forecast of its own. There are no employees; the service is run entirely by "
"the sole operator."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Acceptance of terms"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By accessing Snowdesk at snowdesk.info, you agree to these Terms of Service. "
"If you do not agree, please do not use the service."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. The service"
msgstr ""

msgid "Snowdesk provides:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A viewer for avalanche bulletins published by SLF (Switzerland), ALBINA / "
"EUREGIO (Tyrol, South Tyrol, Trentino) and Météo-France (the French ranges)"
msgstr ""

msgid "An interactive map showing current avalanche danger ratings by region"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An RSS feed per country, which lists each bulletin as it is published and "
"needs no account"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An optional free account, which holds the places and regions you pin, the "
"routes and trips you save, and the map areas you download to read offline"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snowdesk is provided free of charge. I reserve the right to change, suspend, "
"or discontinue any part of the service at any time without notice."
msgstr ""

msgid "4. Safety — please read this"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Avalanche bulletins are a forecast tool, not a guarantee of safe conditions. "
"Snowdesk is an information service only — it does not replace the official "
"bulletin published by the avalanche warning service for the region you are "
"in, professional avalanche training, or your own assessment of conditions in "
"the field."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snowdesk aims to render each bulletin in full — every danger rating, "
"avalanche problem and comment the issuing service published. Nothing is "
"withheld or summarised away. It remains an information service: the "
"avalanche warning service that issued the bulletin is the authority on it, "
"and every bulletin page links back to the official source so you can check "
"it for yourself."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Avalanche conditions change rapidly and vary with aspect, elevation, and "
"recent weather. No digital service can capture every local hazard."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before entering avalanche terrain, you should:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Check the official bulletin for the region you are heading to — the European "
"avalanche warning services are indexed at <a class=\"underline\" "
"href=\"https://www.avalanches.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" "
">avalanches.org</a>"
msgstr ""

msgid "Seek current local knowledge from guides, hut keepers, or ski patrol"
msgstr ""

msgid "Make your own on-site assessment of conditions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Your safety in the mountains is your own responsibility."
msgstr ""

msgid "5. Intellectual property"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Snowdesk's original content — including the interface, design, and copy — is "
"owned by Hugo Rodger-Brown. You may view it for personal, non-commercial "
"use. You may not reproduce, redistribute, or republish it without permission."
msgstr ""

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The avalanche bulletin data displayed on Snowdesk is published by three "
"avalanche warning services — the <a class=\"underline\" href=\"https://www."
"slf.ch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" >WSL Institute for Snow and "
"Avalanche Research SLF</a>, <a class=\"underline\" href=\"https://avalanche."
"report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" >ALBINA / EUREGIO</a> and <a "
"class=\"underline\" href=\"https://meteofrance.com/meteo-montagne\" "
"target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" >Météo-France</a>. The SLF and ALBINA "
